  bubbles: true })` at `.box` and `await new Promise(resolve =>
  setTimeout(resolve, 0))` afterward, since the library's `onDrop` is
  async (per the task doc and the existing DT-003 test's pattern,
  extended here from a bare `await Promise.resolve()` to a macrotask
  wait since `handleItems`'s fallback-to-`files` path still crosses at
  least one microtask boundary via its own `await`, and a `setTimeout`
  wait is a safer margin than counting microtask hops by hand).
- Files changed: `src/index.ts`, `test/index.ts`, `src/AGENTS.md`,
  `specs/drop-target.json` (DT-004 `passes: true`).
- Tests: 2 new tape tests (6 new assertions). Full `npm test` (lint +
  build + typecheck + tape-run) passes with 133 total assertions.
- No "verify in browser" step was listed in DT-004's acceptance
  criteria, so none was performed.
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - `npm run build`'s typecheck step can fail in ways the targeted
    tape-run tests never exercise (esbuild transpiles TS structurally
    and doesn't do full type inference). Don't treat a passing
    `npx vitest`/tape-run subset as proof the story is done -- always
    run the full `npm test` (or at least `tsc --noEmit -p
    tsconfig.json`) before marking a story passing, per the session's
    own TEST-FIRST/TARGETED-TESTING rules.
  - See the new `src/AGENTS.md` entry for the `Object.values(...).find`
    -> `unknown` typecheck gotcha; it will likely recur anywhere else
